hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22179","Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Zakariyya, narrated to us, and Waki' narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Yahya, in his hadith: Amir narrated to me, from Kharijah ibn al-Salt, Yahya said: al-Tamimi, from his uncle, that he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then returned from him. He passed by people with a madman bound in iron among them. His family said: We were told that this companion of yours has brought good; has he anything to treat him. He said: I treated him with the Opening of the Book. Waki' said: Three days, each day twice. He recovered, and they gave me a hundred sheep. I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him. He said: Take them; by my life, whoever ate by a false incantation, you have eaten by a true incantation."
"22180","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Sha'bi, from Kharijah ibn al-Salt, from his uncle, who said: We came from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and came upon a tribe of Arabs. They said: We were told you came from this man with good; have you medicine or an incantation, for we have an insane man in fetters. He said: We said: Yes. He said: They brought the insane man in fetters. He said: I recited the Opening of the Book three days, morning and evening, gathering my saliva then spitting. He said: It was as if he was released from bonds. He said: They gave me a wage. I said: Not until I ask the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I asked him, and he said: Eat; by my life, whoever ate by a false incantation, you have eaten by a true incantation."
